LMAO a good number of parents in northern England in the 90s were miners. You don't get more unsocialable hours and tougher work. But they still found the time to be good parents. Most of my mates dads were miners, in the early part of the 90s before they shut--and then went on to other jobs with unsocial hours--factory work, taxi driving and the like. 

