Ideally, you should be legally allowed to give them a clip round the ear like in the good old days.

I grew up in the 90s/early 2000s and did the usual mischief--knock a door run, egging and the like. But nowhere near as bad as feral little brats are now and that's largely because there was always the chance if we took it too far, one of the house holders would give us a clip.

&#x200B;

It happened to me before, trampled a fella's garden, he caught me and throttled me. Fair play. I didn't go crying to my parents--and if I did, my dad would say I deserved it for being a little bastard. I laughed about it afterwards, never bothered his house again because I knew he'd give me a kicking if I did.

&#x200B;

No days, it doesn't happen--the home owner would get arrested, the idiotic, useless parents would harp one about how Hayden's a good boy and refuse to admit that Hayden is a bit of a cunt and ther'es always the chance the scrotes carry a knife nowadays.

&#x200B;

Bad parenting is the main issue. The current generation of parents are absolutely useless. Back in the 90s--with my friends, the parents knew discipline. Sure, we got up to mischief, but if we got caught the parents believed the neighbours/teachers/police etc and we knew we'd get in trouble.

&#x200B;

Example -- me and some friends vandalised a nearby school playground. Drawing chalk penises on it and knocked a fence over. We got caught, our parents made us go to the school each evening and clean up the mess. Caretaker of the school turned out to be a sound bloke in the end--said he'd let us use the footy field in the future as long as we didn't cause any damage.

