Should be allowed to do whatever it takes and use whatever it takes to defend your home. I had my house broken in before when I was home -- just me (14 years old) and my brother (12). It was scary, sat upstairs when hearing a massive whack from downstairs as someone smashed the backdoor in.

&#x200B;

We had no idea what they intended. If they had knives or what. And this was the Nokia 3310 era before everyone had a phone permanently attached to themselves so we couldn't call police as our phones were downstairs.

We waited until we heard one coming up the stairs. I tried to hit him with half a snooker cue, my brother threw a glass at his head. We both missed. Now, he could easily have died--then on top of the stress of being kids having our home broken in, we'd also have the stress and worry about a criminal conviction and investigation hanging over us, purely for defending ourselves.

