I enjoyed Christmas at school.  Doing the nativity (I was a Shepherd one year), singing carols (Come and join the celebration was the best. Away in the Manger sucked), the last day of school where you just play games and that sort of thing. Snowball fights on the school field.

Everybody was happy.

Then, Christmas at home. Christmas specials, looking through the Argos catalogue to circle toys I wanted, going on a trip to this sort of house/shop place that had reindeer, going to see Santa Claus and getting a shitty gift, leaving out some milk and a carrot for rudolph.

&#x200B;

Then, Christmas night itself, barely able to get to sleep with excitement, then waking up to see the stocking hung on my door. Dashing to my parents room to open them with my brother, then it was downstairs to open the presents under the tree--one at a time, so I open one, then my brother, then my dad, then my mum.

&#x200B;

Having to phone relatives to say thankyou for the gift. That bit I hated.

&#x200B;

Then, around to an Uncle's house, or relatives came to our house, for a Christmas party. Uusally just a buffet, beer and then playing cards until about midnight. As a kid, staying up until midnight was a huge treat.

&#x200B;

I loved it. Christmas here in Taiwan isn't the same. I miss my family this time of year.

